Transitive dependencies
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The MCP server's runtime dependency tree (the parts it imports are bundled into the Lambda
function by esbuild) contains about 95 packages, all under permissive licenses (MIT, ISC,
BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause). The infra/ runtime set contains Apache-2.0, MIT, ISC and
BlueOak-1.0.0 (minimatch) packages, plus "case" (bundled in aws-cdk-lib), dual-licensed
MIT OR GPL-3.0-or-later and used under MIT. The infra/ packages themselves run on the
deployer's machine at synth time; the only parts deployed to AWS are the custom-resource
Lambda handlers and layers shipped inside aws-cdk-lib (e.g. S3 BucketDeployment with its
AWS CLI layer, S3 auto-delete, default security group restriction) and cdk-ecr-deployment
(image copy), all distributed under Apache-2.0 by those projects.
No GPL, LGPL or AGPL licensed packages are used under those licenses.

